# Host ports for the local stack. Copy to `.env` and edit when something on this
# machine already owns one of the defaults; `.env` is gitignored, and Compose
# reads it automatically, so `make up` then needs no flags.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# These are HOST-side only. Service-to-service traffic always uses the canonical
# container ports over the private Compose network (clickhouse:8123,
# collector:4317, collector:9090), so moving one changes the URL you type and
# nothing about the pipeline.
#
# Every one of them binds to 127.0.0.1 and that is not configurable: the local
# boundary is deliberate (DEC-A4 defers TLS, so nothing may listen on a routable
# interface) and invariant 09 fails the build if a mapping loses the prefix.
#
# Keep all five distinct — invariant 03 fails the build on a duplicate host port.
#
# A variable set in the environment or on the make line wins over this file:
#
#   make up FLOW_UI_HOST_PORT=8081

# ClickHouse HTTP interface and the /play query UI.
CLICKHOUSE_HOST_PORT=8123

# The collector's OTLP gRPC receiver, for telemetry sent from the host. The
# generator does not use it: `make generate` runs inside the Compose network and
# speaks to collector:4317 directly.
COLLECTOR_OTLP_HOST_PORT=4317

# The collector's Prometheus /metrics endpoint. `make up` proves the collector
# ready by polling it, so this is the one host port the stack itself depends on.
COLLECTOR_METRICS_HOST_PORT=9090

# flow-ui — the pipeline watching itself (four boards over /metrics + bronze/silver).
FLOW_UI_HOST_PORT=8080

# HyperDX (ADR-0011) — search, traces and dashboards straight over ClickHouse.
# 8082 rather than 8081 so that 8081 stays free as the obvious second choice when
# 8080 is taken, including for moving flow-ui itself.
HYPERDX_HOST_PORT=8082

# ── Local-development login (ClickHouse + HyperDX) ───────────────────────────
# A generic credential for a PERSON to type into the two UIs. LOCAL DEVELOPMENT
# ONLY: the password below is published in this repository, every port binds to
# 127.0.0.1 and TLS is deferred (DEC-2026-10-06-local-scope). Never reuse it for
# anything reachable from another machine, and never ship it to a deployed target.
#
#   ClickHouse   user  sentinel_dev_u   (fixed: it is created by migration 0010)
#                pass  SENTINEL_DEV_PASSWORD
#                where http://127.0.0.1:8123/play · clickhouse-client · curl
#                reads SELECT on bronze.* and silver.* plus system.tables and
#                      system.columns; `readonly = 2`, so no writes, no DDL and
#                      no access management
#   HyperDX      email SENTINEL_DEV_EMAIL
#                pass  SENTINEL_DEV_PASSWORD
#                where http://127.0.0.1:8082 (create it once with `make hyperdx-seed`;
#                      HyperDX 2.40.0 cannot be seeded from the environment)
#
# The two logins are independent systems that happen to share one password: HyperDX
# keeps its account in its own Mongo and connects to ClickHouse as the separate
# SELECT-only service user `sentinel_hyperdx_u`, not as this one.
#
# This is an addition, not a replacement: the collector, flow-ui, HyperDX and the
# migrator keep their least-privilege users and the gitignored password file
# `infra/secrets/ch_password`.
#
# The ClickHouse password is applied ONCE, when migration 0010 first runs
# (`make migrate`, part of `make up`). Changing it afterwards does not rotate an
# existing user:
#   docker compose exec clickhouse clickhouse-client -q \
#     "ALTER USER sentinel_dev_u IDENTIFIED WITH sha256_password BY '<new>'"
# HyperDX needs 12-72 characters with upper and lower case, a digit and one of
# !@#$%^&*(),.?":{}|<>;-+= ; avoid ' " \ and spaces so the value survives the shell
# and the JSON that `make hyperdx-seed` posts.
#
# Resolution: make line / environment, then this file (the Makefile reads these two
# keys from `.env`). The password has NO default: pick your own (12-72 chars, rules
# above) before `make up` / `make migrate` / `make hyperdx-seed`.
SENTINEL_DEV_PASSWORD=
SENTINEL_DEV_EMAIL=dev@sentinel.local
